{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":15,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Matt.15","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Matthew","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Matthew 15","reference":"Matthew 15","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":2,"text":"Mark vii, 1.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":3,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":4,"text":"The elders - The chief doctors or, teachers among the Jews.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":5,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":6,"text":"They wash not their hands when they eat bread - Food in general is termed bread in Hebrew; so that to eat bread is the same as to make a meal.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":7,"text":"4. honour thy father and mother - Which implies all such relief as they stand in need of.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":8,"text":"Exod. xx, 12; xxi, 17.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":9,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":10,"text":"It is a gift by whatsoever thou mightest have been profited by me - That is, I have given, or at least, purpose to give to the treasury of the temple, what you might otherwise have had from me.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":11,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":12,"text":"Well did Isaiah prophesy of you, saying - That is, the description which Isaiah gave of your fathers, is exactly applicable to you.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":13,"text":"The words therefore which were a description of them, are a prophecy with regard to you.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":14,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":15,"text":"Their heart is far from me - And without this all outward worship is mere mockery of God.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":16,"text":"Isaiah xxix, 13.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":17,"text":"9.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":18,"text":"Teaching the commandments of men - As equal with, nay, superior to, those of God.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":19,"text":"What can be a more heinous sin?","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":20,"text":"13.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":21,"text":"Every plant - That is, every doctrine.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":22,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":23,"text":"Let them alone - If they are indeed blind leaders of the blind; let them alone: concern not yourselves about them: a plain direction how to behave with regard to all such.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":24,"text":"Luke vi, 39.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":25,"text":"17.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":26,"text":"Are ye also yet without understanding - How fair and candid are the sacred historians?","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":27,"text":"Never concealing or excusing their own blemishes.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":28,"text":"19.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":29,"text":"First evil thoughts - then murders - and the rest.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":30,"text":"Railings - The Greek word includes all reviling, backbiting, and evil speaking.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":31,"text":"21.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":21,"scriptureVerseEnd":21},{"verse":32,"text":"Mark vii, 24.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":21,"scriptureVerseEnd":21},{"verse":33,"text":"22.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":34,"text":"A woman of Canaan - Canaan was also called Syrophenicia, as lying between Syria properly so called, and Phenicia, by the sea side.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":35,"text":"Cried to him - From afar, Thou Son of David - So she had some knowledge of the promised Messiah.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":36,"text":"23.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":37,"text":"He answered her not a word - He sometimes tries our faith in like manner.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":38,"text":"24.","sourceParagraph":16,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":39,"text":"I am not sent - Not primarily; not yet.","sourceParagraph":16,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":40,"text":"25.","sourceParagraph":17,"scriptureVerseStart":25,"scriptureVerseEnd":25},{"verse":41,"text":"Then came she - Into the house where he now was.","sourceParagraph":17,"scriptureVerseStart":25,"scriptureVerseEnd":25},{"verse":42,"text":"28.","sourceParagraph":18,"scriptureVerseStart":28,"scriptureVerseEnd":28},{"verse":43,"text":"Thy faith - Thy reliance on the power and goodness of God.","sourceParagraph":18,"scriptureVerseStart":28,"scriptureVerseEnd":28},{"verse":44,"text":"29.","sourceParagraph":19,"scriptureVerseStart":29,"scriptureVerseEnd":29},{"verse":45,"text":"The sea of Galilee - The Jews gave the name of seas to all large lakes.","sourceParagraph":19,"scriptureVerseStart":29,"scriptureVerseEnd":29},{"verse":46,"text":"This was a hundred furlongs long, and forty broad.","sourceParagraph":19,"scriptureVerseStart":29,"scriptureVerseEnd":29},{"verse":47,"text":"It was called also, the sea of Tiberias.","sourceParagraph":19,"scriptureVerseStart":29,"scriptureVerseEnd":29},{"verse":48,"text":"It lay on the borders of Galilee, and the city of Tiberias stood on its western shore.","sourceParagraph":19,"scriptureVerseStart":29,"scriptureVerseEnd":29},{"verse":49,"text":"It was likewise styled the lake of Gennesareth: perhaps a corruption of Cinnereth, the name by which it was anciently called, Num. xxxiv, 11.","sourceParagraph":19,"scriptureVerseStart":29,"scriptureVerseEnd":29},{"verse":50,"text":"Mark vii, 31.","sourceParagraph":19,"scriptureVerseStart":29,"scriptureVerseEnd":29},{"verse":51,"text":"32.","sourceParagraph":20,"scriptureVerseStart":32,"scriptureVerseEnd":32},{"verse":52,"text":"They continue with me now three days - It was now the third day since they came.","sourceParagraph":20,"scriptureVerseStart":32,"scriptureVerseEnd":32},{"verse":53,"text":"Mark viii, 1.","sourceParagraph":20,"scriptureVerseStart":32,"scriptureVerseEnd":32},{"verse":54,"text":"36.","sourceParagraph":21,"scriptureVerseStart":36,"scriptureVerseEnd":36},{"verse":55,"text":"He gave thanks, or blessed the food - That is, he praised God for it, and prayed for a blessing upon it.","sourceParagraph":21,"scriptureVerseStart":36,"scriptureVerseEnd":36}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Matthew","chapter":15}}